CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE sp(para_production_type_code text, para_parent_product_id integer, para_town_city text, para_login_name text) LANGUAGE plpgsql AS $$
DECLARE
    ref_cursor CURSOR FOR SELECT * FROM "Products";
    rec RECORD;
    ref_cursor2 CURSOR FOR SELECT * FROM "Customers";
    rec2 RECORD;
    matched_products integer := 0;
    matched_customers integer := 0;
BEGIN
    OPEN ref_cursor;
    LOOP
        FETCH ref_cursor INTO rec;
        EXIT WHEN NOT FOUND;
        IF {SLOT_1} THEN
            UPDATE "Products" SET "parent_product_id" = {SLOT_2} WHERE CURRENT OF ref_cursor;
            matched_products := {SLOT_3};
        END IF;
    END LOOP;
    CLOSE ref_cursor;

    IF {SLOT_4} THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'No Products rows match production_type_code %', para_production_type_code;
    END IF;

    OPEN ref_cursor2;
    LOOP
        FETCH ref_cursor2 INTO rec2;
        EXIT WHEN NOT FOUND;
        IF {SLOT_5} THEN
            UPDATE "Customers" SET "login_name" = {SLOT_6} WHERE CURRENT OF ref_cursor2;
            matched_customers := {SLOT_7};
        END IF;
    END LOOP;
    CLOSE ref_cursor2;

    IF {SLOT_8} THEN
        RAISE EXCEPTION 'No Customers rows match town_city %', para_town_city;
    END IF;
END;
$$;

## Slots

### {SLOT_1}
Kind: condition
What must go there: A Boolean condition that is true when the current ProductCatalog row's `production_type_code` column, read through the cursor record variable `rec`, and the procedure parameter `para_production_type_code` meet the cold-lock condition.

### {SLOT_3}
Kind: assignment
What must go there: The right-hand side expression that increments the product match counter by one. It must evaluate to the current value of the `matched_products` variable plus one. The template already includes the assignment target and assignment operator, so this slot contains only the arithmetic expression.

### {SLOT_4}
Kind: condition
What must go there: A Boolean condition that is true when the product match counter variable `matched_products` is exactly equal to zero. This controls whether the procedure raises the no-match exception for ProductCatalog.

### {SLOT_5}
Kind: condition
What must go there: A Boolean condition that is true when the current Customers row's `town_city` column, read through the cursor record variable `rec2`, is exactly equal to the procedure parameter `para_town_city`. Use exact equality comparison, not a null-safe comparison, so a null in either the column or the parameter must make the condition false.

### {SLOT_6}
Kind: value
What must go there: The value to assign to the Customers row's `login_name` column in the UPDATE statement. It is simply the procedure parameter `para_login_name`.

### {SLOT_8}
Kind: condition
What must go there: A Boolean condition that is true when the customer match counter variable `matched_customers` meets the cold-lock condition. This controls whether the procedure raises the no-match exception for Customers.

